cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CamoGED: Camouflage — Generation, Evaluation, Detection"
message: "If you use CamoGED, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "MichaelCSHN"
    given-names: ""
    # TODO: replace with full legal name and ORCID before release
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MichaelCSHN/CamoGED"
url: "https://github.com/MichaelCSHN/CamoGED"
abstract: >-
  CamoGED is a cross-domain open platform covering camouflage generation,
  detection, and evaluation across the natural-science, military, and
  humanities/art perspectives and the physical, digital, and intelligent
  technical domains. It comprises an online monograph, a curated Awesome list,
  an aggregator website (papers, model zoo, leaderboard, demos, datasets), and
  a unified evaluation toolkit (camo-eval).
keywords:
  - camouflage
  - camouflaged object detection
  - adversarial camouflage
  - concealment
  - computer vision
  - benchmark
  - survey
